    q11392: { h: "1cf781f44d9c", text: "Iron ore goes from the mine to the steel plant on a long contract, with a grade test on every consignment: would you like the world of big contracts?" },
    q11393: { h: "12f10707584f", text: "Coal is sold by bidding in an e-auction; the transport cost is added to the price: will you manage adding the bid and the freight?" },
    q11394: { h: "ce022dd2ee2b", text: "Gold is bought and sold through a bullion dealer at the printed rate; the game of the tola is fine: would you read the rate board every day?" },
    q11395: { h: "8a09ed4f0144", text: "Diamonds are judged and sold in parcels; a deal of trust is sealed with a handshake: would you enjoy a market of judgement and trust?" },
    q11396: { h: "5265f3b9d1d1", text: "Copper sells at the rate of the metal exchange; scrap copper has a separate market: will you weigh both new and old metal?" },
    q11397: { h: "887f5e7fc9fe", text: "Lithium deals are made with battery companies on contracts of years: would you read the contracts of the metal of the future?" },
    q11398: { h: "a476cced0b99", text: "Cobalt is exported with a test report; purity is the price: does selling with a report appeal to you?" },
    q11399: { h: "1d4a664e5b82", text: "Stainless steel mills take nickel on contract; the rate changes with the world price: will you keep up with the news of metal prices?" },
    q11400: { h: "b1644cdb7c11", text: "From bauxite to aluminium there is a different buyer at every stage: would you understand selling link by link?" },
    q11401: { h: "13bca0e672cf", text: "Uranium is sold only to a buyer with government permission; papers first, goods later: would you like a trade by permission?" },
    q11402: { h: "b2a84cf0519f", text: "The buyers of rare minerals are a few countries and companies; the deals are like diplomacy: would you handle a select set of customers?" },
    q11403: { h: "59cc9e065e19", text: "Builders buy granite slabs at a rate per square foot; the price goes by shine and cracks: would you sell after judging the slab?" },
    q11404: { h: "b0f6e25ba47f", text: "Salt in bulk to the iodine plant, in packets as a brand: would you understand the big trade of a cheap thing?" },
    q11405: { h: "d41f224aad18", text: "Phosphate is sold to fertiliser factories by the shipload; the weight at the port is final: will you keep the accounts of ship weights?" },
    q11406: { h: "c8eaebe27b42", text: "Potash is distributed in the country at the import rate; the government subsidy changes the price: would you read a trade tied to policy?" },
    q11407: { h: "3c7fadeb6c1e", text: "The refinery buys crude oil at a rate per barrel; the day's world price is the deal: would you enjoy the arithmetic of barrels?" },
    q11408: { h: "45366e4530ca", text: "Natural gas is sold by pipe meter; the bill is by the unit: does selling by the meter appeal to you?" },
    q11409: { h: "6f4e2e79a94e", text: "LNG is sold on long contracts for ship cargoes; one deal, years of supply: would you understand a giant contract?" },
    q11410: { h: "e1bda6ed6607", text: "The refinery takes crude oil and sells petrol, diesel and gas to many customers: would you handle one purchase and ten sales?" },
