    q11412: { h: "c185c19d8ac9", text: "Pipeline gas is sold by the meter reading, CNG by the pump nozzle: would you run sales in two streams?" },
    q11413: { h: "309f5e5e0bbb", text: "Oil companies buy ethanol at a rate fixed by the government; the quantity is shared out by tender: would you learn selling by tender?" },
    q11414: { h: "cc6ef2497882", text: "Transport fleets fill up with bio-diesel on contract; used oil is bought from roadside eateries: will you join both ends?" },
    q11415: { h: "6647645c4ceb", text: "A mining service company sells machine hours; the bill is made from the hour meter: would you like the accounts of selling hours?" },
    q11416: { h: "8f6ff8f11648", text: "Oil well services are sold at a day rate; the rate for one day runs into lakhs: would you read contracts with big rates?" },
    q11417: { h: "90380eb0e0a2", text: "Solar power is sold to a government company for 25 years on a PPA contract: does one signature and twenty-five years of sales appeal to you?" },
    q11418: { h: "7c1524f66646", text: "Every unit of wind power is recorded on the meter and sold; if the wind blows, there are earnings: would you enjoy sales tied to the weather?" },
    q11419: { h: "0fd6f2f5743c", text: "State boards buy hydropower; the rainwater itself is the goods: would you understand a contract with nature?" },
    q11420: { h: "24c2fc738c51", text: "Electricity made from geothermal steam goes to the grid at a fixed rate: would you like the idea of selling the heat of the ground?" },
    q11421: { h: "83dcdfc59a0c", text: "A biogas plant buys cow dung and sells both gas cylinders and compost: would you enjoy the two-way earnings from waste?" },
    q11422: { h: "80674dcaa0be", text: "Governments make pilot contracts for tidal power; new technology, new buyers: will you step into a pioneering market?" },
    q11423: { h: "5d59d036d2ec", text: "Fertiliser and steel factories are becoming buyers of green hydrogen; the contracts are being written now: would you take a place in the front row of a new market?", eor: "पहली क़तार पकड़ना = क़तार में जगह लेना (ChatGPT mg02 ऑडिट)" },
    q11424: { h: "4e65aac84bba", text: "Battery storage buys electricity in cheap hours and sells it in costly hours: would you play this game of trading across hours?" },
    q11425: { h: "884015092d09", text: "Solar panels are sold through a dealer network at a rate per watt; government tenders are a separate route: would you run sales on two routes?" },
    q11426: { h: "5b2b264ff0bd", text: "The turbine maker does megawatt deals with the wind farm developer; a service contract is sold along with it: would you like selling machine and service together?" },
    q11427: { h: "9ddd5d70b58c", text: "Jars of drinking water go to shops and offices by count every day, with accounts of empty jars returned: would you handle the count and the returns?" },
    q11428: { h: "d26b65d6e746", text: "Water purifiers are sold to homes on instalments; changing filters brings regular earnings: would you enjoy earnings after the sale?" },
    q11429: { h: "108815ec4603", text: "The municipal corporation buys sewage treatment services by tender, with yearly maintenance attached: would you keep up this work with a government customer?" },
    q11430: { h: "4d2fe2fbdb80", text: "In waste management, housing societies pay a monthly fee; the sorted scrap is sold separately: would you count both the fee and the scrap?" },
    q11431: { h: "60a11458bf3c", text: "A recycling unit buys from the scrap dealer at a rate per kilo, makes granules and sells to factories: would you understand the profit from kilo to granule?" },
    q11432: { h: "048497010584", text: "The resin maker sells to paint and glue factories at a rate per drum; sample approval comes first: will you go from sample to order?" },
    q11433: { h: "f378baa86508", text: "Industrial gas cylinders run on rent plus refill; returning the cylinder is a condition: would you like the way of a rental trade?" },
    q11434: { h: "f3add3fe21c0", text: "Governments and companies buy deep-sea survey services at a day rate: would you read the deals of sea services?" },
    q12342: { h: "57bf232a664f", text: "The raw materials of iron and steel are ore, coking coal and limestone: would you understand ore grades?" },
    q12343: { h: "31758966d397", text: "The materials of the coal business are a mine block and washing water: would you enjoy the subject of coal washing?" },
    q12344: { h: "9c4a75c8bb8a", text: "Gold mining runs on ore rock and leaching chemicals: would you like the link from rock to metal?" },
    q12345: { h: "259f604505ad", text: "The materials of diamond mining are kimberlite rock and sorting mesh: would you understand sorting rock?" },
    q12346: { h: "5a813ff2f494", text: "The copper industry gathers ore concentrate and acid: would you enjoy judging concentrate?" },
    q12347: { h: "ccaa86b01296", text: "The material of the lithium business is salt-lake brine or rock ore: would you like drying brine?" },
    q12348: { h: "ab0820a62004", text: "Cobalt mining needs hand sorting of ore and washing water: would you understand strict supervision?" },
